macros/*_macros-cache.txt
macros/*_macros-cache.html


# Addon Atlas data store (local inventory + macro drafts) - not git-tracked.
addon_atlas/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-11-11 (Tandumonium) - the Flipbook wing.
#
# PUBLIC: _gewey_gui/Flipbook.html. It bakes its own dataset at build time, so
# the page carries every position and event it needs; nothing is fetched at
# runtime.
#
# LOCAL: the engine (Timeline/flipbook_extract.py + flipbook_render.py) and the
# extracted dataset (Timeline/data/flipbook.json) live under Timeline/, which is
# already covered by Timeline/.gitignore = `*`.
#
# PUBLIC as well, and this line used to be wrong: the screenshot thumbnails in
# _gewey_gui/_shots/. Flipbook.html embeds each of them as a page-relative
# <img src="_shots/<shot>.jpg"> -- that is the filmstrip, the sticky photo pane
# and the photo pins on the canvas. Ignoring the folder meant the page shipped
# 61 references to files no published copy of the repo carries, so every
# photograph 404'd on the site while the local build looked perfect. The
# originals stay on Z: in Screenshots/; these 480px derivatives (~45 KB each)
# travel with the page. Rebuild with:
#   python Timeline/flipbook_extract.py && python Timeline/flipbook_render.py
# then commit the page together with any new thumbnails it references --
# tests/test_published_assets.py fails if a published page points at a file the
# repo does not carry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-11-16 (Tandumonium, "Tandu Legacy" wide retail pass).
#
# PUBLIC this pass - read by the new pane and by every nav:
#   _gewey_gui/tandu_legacy.html    new wing; self-contained, no runtime fetch
#   _gewey_gui/index.html           new sidebar button "iTanduLegacy"
#   _gewey_gui/_fuhevva_evva.html   home card linking the wing
# Everything the page displays is embedded at build time; it fetches nothing,
# so no data file has to ship beside it.
#
# LOCAL this pass - probes and payloads, no page points at them:
#   Research/_local/_retail_legacy_scan.py   walks all 54 retail folders
#   Research/_local/_legacy_api_probe.py     Raider.IO + Wayback CDX
#   Research/_local/_legacy_web_probe.py     SERP probe (returned noise)
#   Research/_local/_wire_nav.py             nav wiring, idempotent
#   Research/_local/_link_audit.py           every local href must resolve
#   Research/_raw/retail_legacy.json         per-folder census (58 KB)
#   Research/_raw/legacy_api_probe.json      captures + profiles
#   Research/_raw/legacy_web_probe.json      SERP dump
# Research/_local/ and Research/_raw/ already cover the four scripts and three
# JSON files, so this section exists to STATE the rule, not to widen it.
#
# The one new pattern is deliberate: Wayback captures are somebody else's HTML.
# They are evidence, never assets - the same rule the armory_* patterns below
# already enforce.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Research/_raw/wayback_*
**/wayback_*.html
**/wayback_*.json

